/-!
# The attached elliptic eigenform is new

Theorem statement: `HorizontalPadicL.attachedEigenform_isNew`
(`cd9c443b-2229-4eb9-a9e1-5536956a795f`), by davidloeffler, 2026-10-08.

Proof: submission `b91c5b2b-ffeb-453f-a823-d27ed5f38fdb`, by davidloeffler, 2026-10-08 (ACCEPTED);
locally adapted.

Let E be a modular elliptic curve over the rationals, let N be its least modular level, and fix a
complex embedding ι of the algebraic closure of the rationals. The specific weight-two eigenform f_E
attached to E at level N is new:

$$ f_E \text{ is new at level } N. $$

Here newness means that its Fourier expansion cannot occur as a weight-two cusp form at any smaller
positive Γ₀ level. This result applies to the explicitly defined attached eigenform, whose
coefficients are the arithmetic L-series coefficients of E and whose nebentype is trivial.

## Explanation of the source proof

The explicitly attached form is new at its least modular level N. If the same Fourier expansion
occurred at a positive smaller level M, that cusp form would exhibit modularity of E at M. This
contradicts the defining minimality of N. The algebraic Fourier coefficients of the attached form
are exactly E.LFunction(n), so the comparison is with the chosen form rather than an existential
witness.

